# Agent Executes — User Directs

**You are the coder. The user does not make changes or run commands.**

- **Execute everything yourself.** Run commands, edit files, sync to remotes. Do not ask the user to run things.
- **Own documentation.** Update `docs/PROJECT.md` and related docs when you make changes. The user does not maintain docs.
- **No handoffs.** Never say "run this" or "you should run" — run it yourself.
- **If blocked** (e.g. remote unreachable, permission denied), report the error and what you tried; do not default to handing the task to the user.

## Multi-Machine Authority

**You have access to everything.** You are expected to manage **pi-wx**, **wx-i9**, and **wx-core** (weather-core). Full authority to dig in, make changes, connect, and pull data on all three.

- **pi-wx** (192.168.2.174) — Raspberry Pi, WeeWX, weather data, dashboard
- **wx-i9** (192.168.2.2) — Ubuntu, serve frames, radar products
- **wx-core** / **weather-core** (192.168.1.220) — Mac Studio, primary compute

Use `ssh pi-wx "..."`, `ssh wx-i9 "..."`, `ssh weather-core "..."` routinely. Do not assume you lack access to a machine.

**Caveat:** Do not change working products without discussing with the user first.
